# .percolate-ignore for the coordinator-claude-publish-repo-toplevel flat-mirror target.
#
# Files listed here are protected in BOTH directions:
#   Phase 1 (src→dst): not synced from source (we don't carry them in dist/).
#   Phase 2 (dst delete-not-in-source): protected from deletion in the publish repo root.
#
# These are publish-repo-owned infrastructure files, NOT content we originate.
# The publish repo authors them locally; Claude Central does not back-percolate them.

# The .percolate-ignore file itself shouldn't appear in the publish repo root —
# it's a source-side control file, not OSS-facing content.
.percolate-ignore

# README-meta.md explains the dist/ namespace to EM sessions in Claude Central
# — internal documentation, not OSS-facing content. Names Claude Central's
# repo layout and source paths that should not appear at the publish repo root.
README-meta.md

# Publish-repo's own gitignore patterns (different from Claude Central's gitignore).
.gitignore

# Publish-repo's Python venv pin (per-publish-repo, not authored here).
.python-version

# Publish-repo's CLAUDE.md is the depersonalized OSS-facing variant of our doctrine.
# Today it's authored in the publish repo; back-percolating it is a separate decision
# (would require running depersonalize-for-publish.sh against ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md and
# placing the output here). Deferred — protect for now.
CLAUDE.md
